From: radiance-web EnergyPlus WASM port
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] third_party/fmt-8.0.1: disable FMT_CONSTEVAL for clang >= 15

What: for `FMT_CLANG_VERSION >= 1500`, `#define FMT_CONSTEVAL` to empty,
disabling fmt 8's consteval compile-time format-string check for that
compiler branch (the pre-existing gcc>=10 / clang 11.0-14.99 branch is
untouched).

Why (toolchain, not physics): fmt 8.0.1's `consteval basic_format_string`
check interacts badly with clang >= 15 (a hard "call to consteval function is
not a constant expression" error surfaces from format-inl.h via FMT_STRING
call sites in EnergyPlus). Disabling consteval only removes the COMPILE-TIME
format-string validation pass; runtime formatting behavior (the actual string
output) is unchanged for every call site, matching call site, in the codebase.

Applies to: energyplus-src/third_party/fmt-8.0.1/include/fmt/core.h
Apply with (-p1, from the pristine energyplus-src/ tree root):
  patch -p1 < patches/energyplus/0004-fmt8-consteval-clang15.patch

--- a/third_party/fmt-8.0.1/include/fmt/core.h
+++ b/third_party/fmt-8.0.1/include/fmt/core.h
@@ -293,7 +293,13 @@
 #endif
 
 #ifndef FMT_CONSTEVAL
-#  if ((FMT_GCC_VERSION >= 1000 || FMT_CLANG_VERSION >= 1101) && \
+#  if FMT_CLANG_VERSION >= 1500
+// fmt 8's consteval basic_format_string interacts badly with clang >= 15
+// (hard error "call to consteval function is not a constant expression" in
+// format-inl.h via FMT_STRING). Disabling consteval only removes the
+// compile-time format-string check; runtime formatting is unchanged.
+#    define FMT_CONSTEVAL
+#  elif ((FMT_GCC_VERSION >= 1000 || FMT_CLANG_VERSION >= 1101) && \
        __cplusplus > 201703L) ||                                 \
       (defined(__cpp_consteval) &&                               \
        !FMT_MSC_VER)  // consteval is broken in MSVC.
